## Implemented route-complete contract

- [x] Replace single-halfedge repair candidates with exact maximal route chains between shared authoritative corners.
- [x] Include complete canonical interval identities, geometric support, affected patches/domains, and component/sheet scope.
- [x] Generate a topology-derived coupled-sector interval union when multiple differing routes belong to one unresolved relationship.
- [x] Evaluate the coupled candidate before individual complete routes without arbitrary subset enumeration.
- [x] Subdivide every interval in one atomic twin-conforming transaction.
- [x] Commit only when assembly succeeds and exact ownership conflicts reach zero.
- [x] Reject persistent, replacement, repeated, incomplete, invalid, or exhausted route transactions fail-closed.
- [x] Preserve one invocation-owned non-recursive ledger and exact repair-state equality.
- [x] Release superseded descriptors, completed patches, assembly storage, candidate storage, and repeated failure strings.
- [x] Keep at most one live mutable candidate complex.
- [x] Add route identities, interval lists, compound insertion/split totals, affected domains, outcomes, and owned-byte diagnostics to pipeline hashes and benchmark JSON.
- [x] Replace vacuous structural fixtures with an authoritative same-corner route fixture and assert the initial conflict precondition.
- [x] Add an already-successful negative control that requires zero repair work.

No final-face deduplication, positional vertex merge, source-triangle pairing, source-grid recovery, legacy fallback, arbitrary powerset search, patch/halfedge-ID special case, or validator weakening was introduced.

